  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Anna decides to go jogging. Her position from the starting point, measured in meters, is given by the function $s(t),$ where $t$ is the time in seconds. The values of $s(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ | $7$ | $9$ | $11$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $s(t)$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $14$ | $25$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nApproximate the velocity ${s}^{′}(t)$ at the point $t=7$ using a central difference approximation with the step size $h=2.$",
